usage: record_ros_outputs.py [-h] --bag BAG --outdir OUTDIR --config CONFIG
                             [--vehicle-id VEHICLE_ID] [--rate RATE]
                             [--timeout TIMEOUT]
                             [--ready-timeout READY_TIMEOUT]
                             [--drain-seconds DRAIN_SECONDS]
                             [--artifact ARTIFACT]

Run the real ROS node, installed official checker and result recorder. The
shell entry point is tools/ros_reference_check.sh. Outputs include raw bags,
checker/node/player/recorder logs, effective parameters, normalized candidate
CSV, independent offline metrics, and run_summary.json. No reference relay is
started. The checker package must already be installed in the ROS environment.

options:
  -h, --help            show this help message and exit
  --bag BAG
  --outdir OUTDIR       New or empty directory; existing results are never
                        overwritten
  --config CONFIG
  --vehicle-id VEHICLE_ID
  --rate RATE
  --timeout TIMEOUT     Maximum wall seconds after playback resumes; timeout
                        is a failed partial run
  --ready-timeout READY_TIMEOUT
  --drain-seconds DRAIN_SECONDS
  --artifact ARTIFACT
